Hi all,

I've noticed that a fairly common question being asked around here is
"where is the API documentation?", and the answer is usually something
along the lines of "see the examples, then write some yourself".  I've
written up a document that explains some of the basics, and may be
helpful for novice bluez developers.

http://people.csail.mit.edu/albert/pubs/ashuang-sm-thesis-2005.pdf

These are the parts that I think bluez programmers might care about

chapter 2 is a high level overview of bluetooth programming.  No code.
chapter 3 is an introduction to developing applications in PyBluez
chapter 4 is an introduction to developing applications in bluez

Since it has an academic slant, it's nowhere near complete, and puts
heavy emphasis on some things that may seem insignificant.  If there's
interest, though, I'd consider expanding chapter 4 into something to
point beginner developers to.  Corrections and comments are also
welcome, as I am quite aware that I am by no means an expert at this
yet.

Regards,
Albert


